A||||2||rodmcneill||CD changer hookup.||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-27-2001||09:57 PM||||I am thinking about putting a CD changer in my Fiero. I am keeping my stock radio-cassette player. How do the changers hook up to the stock radio?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-27-2001||10:24 PM||||Most aftermarket cd changers have an option if you want to use them with your stock radio.  They use FM modulation to play through the radio.  If you were using, say, a JVC head unit, you would just by the JVC changer that you wanted and then would plug it in, and play the sound directly through the radio.  But, since you arent doing that, make sure that you get a changer that "FM modulates"   All you do is set the little modulating unit to whatever radio station isnt used in your area, and then tune the radio to it when the unit is playing.  We had one in our van, a pioneer unit that modulated, and I couldn't tell much difference, the signal is pretty strong so you get very good sound.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||01-27-2001||10:58 PM||||Yes, I have an FM modulated unit in my Fiero.  They are pretty simple to install.  You plug the antenna cable from the car into the modulator.  It has an antenna 'pigtail' that then gets plugged into the car radio's antenna input jack.  Provide power to the FM modulator (switched and constant 12V) and then connect the supplied cable between the modulator and the CD changer.  The wiring is pretty simple.  There is usually an additional cable that plugs into the modulator and then into a remote control unit.  I have a station preset on my radio for the CD player.<P>Hardest part is finding a place to mount the changer.  Some have them behind the seat.  I originally mounted mine in the rear cargo area and ran the cable thru the firewall in a rubber plug above (or below?) the ECM.  Since it took up so much precious space back there, I have since built a plywood 'shelf' in the front area that sits over the spare tire.  The CD changer is mounted to the shelf and 'hangs' down over the spare tire.  Works great.....<P>||||reg||1
